  "title": "87: Al-A'laa الأعلى",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "There are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated that the reciter of this Surah will get the reward equal to ten times the number of letters in the divine books that were revealed to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), Prophet Ibrahim (a.s.) and Prophet Musa (a.s.). It is also said that in the hereafter, he will be told to enter Jannah through whichever door he pleases.\nImam Ali (a.s.) used to recite this Surah often in his compulsory prayers. Surah al-A’ala is also good for relieving ear pains and other ailments.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nسَبِّحِ اسْمَ رَبِّكَ الْاَعْلَىۙ‏(1)\nSABBEH ISME RABBEKAL A-A’LAL.\nGlorify the name of thy Guardian-Lord Most High, \nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَ فَسَوّٰى ۙ‏(2)\nLAZEE KHALAQA FASAWWAA.\nWho hath created, and further, given order and proportion; \nوَالَّذِىْ قَدَّرَ فَهَدٰى ۙ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEE QADDARA FA-HADAA.\nWho hath ordained laws. And granted guidance; \nوَالَّذِىْۤ اَخْرَجَ الْمَرْعٰى ۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAZEE AKHRAJAL MAR-A’A.\nAnd Who bringeth out the (green and luscious) pasture, \nفَجَعَلَهٗ غُثَآءً اَحْوٰىؕ‏(5)\nFA-JA-A’LAHU GHOSAAA-AN AHWAA.\nAnd then doth make it (but) swarthy stubble. \nسَنُقْرِئُكَ فَلَا تَنْسٰٓىۙ‏(6)\nSANUQRE-OKA FALAA TANSAA.\nBy degrees shall We teach thee to declare (the Message), so thou shalt not forget, \nاِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّهٗ يَعْلَمُ الْجَهْرَ وَمَا يَخْفٰىؕ‏(7)\nILLAA MAA SHAAA-AL LAAH, INNAHU YA’LAMUL JAHRA WA MAA KAKHFAA.\nExcept as Allah wills: For He knoweth what is manifest and what is hidden. \nوَنُيَسِّرُكَ لِلْيُسْرٰى ۖۚ‏(8)\nWA NOYASSEROKA LIL-YUSRAA.\nAnd We will make it easy for thee (to follow) the simple (Path). \nفَذَكِّرْ اِنْ نَّفَعَتِ الذِّكْرٰىؕ‏(9)\nFA-ZAKKIR IN NAFA-A’TIZ ZIKRAA.\nTherefore give admonition in case the admonition profits (the hearer). \nسَيَذَّكَّرُ مَنْ يَّخْشٰىۙ‏(10)\nSAYAZZAKKARO MAN-Y YAKHSHAA.\nThe admonition will be received by those who fear (Allah): \nوَيَتَجَنَّبُهَا الْاَشْقَىۙ‏(11)\nWA YATAJANNABOHAL ASQAL.\nBut it will be avoided by those most unfortunate ones, \nالَّذِىْ يَصْلَى النَّارَ الْكُبْرٰىۚ‏(12)\nLAZEE YASLAN NAARAL KUBRAA.\nWho will enter the Great Fire, \nثُمَّ لَا يَمُوْتُ فِيْهَا وَلَا يَحْيٰىؕ‏(13)\nSUMMA LAA YAMOOTO FEEHAA WA LAA YAHYAA.\nIn which they will then neither die nor live. \nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ مَنْ تَزَكّٰىۙ‏(14)\nQAD AFLAHA MAN TAZAKKAA.\nBut those will prosper who purify themselves, \nوَذَكَرَ اسْمَ رَبِّهٖ فَصَلّٰى ؕ‏(15)\nWA ZAKARAS MA RABBEHI FA-SALLAA.\nAnd glorify the name of their Guardian-Lord, and (lift their hearts) in prayer. \nبَلْ تُؤْثِرُوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَاۖ‏(16)\nBAL TOA-SEROONAL HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nNay (behold), ye prefer the life of this world; \nوَالْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ وَّ اَبْقٰىؕ‏(17)\nWAL AAKHERATO KHAYRUNW WA ABQAA.\nBut the Hereafter is better and more enduring. \nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَفِى الصُّحُفِ الْاُوْلٰىۙ‏(18)\nINNA HAAZAA LAFIS SOHOFIL OOLAA.\nAnd this is in the Books of the earliest (Revelation), \nصُحُفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَمُوْسٰى‏(19)\nSOHOFE IBRAAHEEMA WA MOOSAA.\nThe Books of Abraham and Moses. "
